    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/project-officer-waite-urrbrae-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Together, we will defineAdelaide University",
      "description": "Project Officer - Waite (Urrbrae), SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Project Officer Waite (Urrbrae), SA, Australia, 5064 Education & Training HEO6 Fixed term - Part-time HEO6 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in the School of Agriculture, Food and Wine, College of Science at the Waite Campus Part-time (0.7FTE), fixed term contract for 3 years Salary starting at $92,511 per annum (pro rata) plus 17% superannuation Work across a major multi-partner research collaboration advancing Australian grains At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Coordinate the delivery of a significant multi-partner research investment focused on accelerating the development of improved wheat and barley varieties through new breeding technologies. You will work closely with scientists and professional staff, communicate with project partners to track progress against a detailed operating plan, arrange project updates, ensure milestones are on schedule, and assemble accurate reports for investment agencies, helping translate research innovation into more resilient crops and meaningful outcomes for Australian grain growers. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description above to discover more about this opportunity. The team Reporting to the Director, Waite Research Institute, you will work within a collaborative multidisciplinary team and engage broadly across Adelaide University, including research services and business development teams. You will also work closely with university, industry and other research partners to coordinate activity and support the successful delivery of this major grains research investment. Visit the AU website to learn more about the School of Agriculture, Food and Wine. Our people This role is ideal for someone who enjoys bringing people together, building trusted relationships and keeping complex projects moving. You will join an inclusive and collaborative team that values flexibility, open communication and shared accountability, with opportunities to work both face-to-face and flexibly while coordinating stakeholders across the University and externally. Experience To thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: A degree or equivalent qualification in science, business or a related discipline, or relevant equivalent experience Demonstrated project management experience, ideally within research, agriculture or another complex multi-partner environment Strong stakeholder management skills, with experience building productive relationships across internal and external organisations Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including project reporting, milestone tracking and coordination of meetings and deliverables Experience using project management systems and coordinating timelines, budgets and resources; knowledge of agricultural or biological sciences would be highly regarded Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Build on your career with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter that tells us why you’re excited about the role The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Tuesday 15 September 2026 Please note that the role description is not attached to this advertisement as it is currently being finalised. For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493324 ) . Georgia Borg Recruitment Consultant +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 98ef7588 Last Name (required) 482f4f3f Email (required) 33991166 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 5fc5ab34 Last Name (required) 168a5674 Email (required) 4b3f64ba Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Senior Lecturer - Psychology Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Psychology Provide clinical oversight, assessment and support for Master of Psychology students undertaking placements Technical Assistant, Hospital and Health Service Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Specialist Facilities and Technical Services - Health Help deliver technical services to support simulation and clinical teaching environments, maintain compliance with safety standards and foster a collaborative team culture. Executive Assistant Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 College Services - Science Manage executive operations, coordination and communications for senior leaders, enabling strategic delivery across the College of Science. Bioinformatics Analyst - Level A Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 SAIGENCI Apply advanced data analysis, statistics, bioinformatics, and computational biology to solve complex biological and biomedical challenges, turning high-dimensional data into actionable insights that drive scientific discovery and impact. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 7d17b341 Last Name (required) 995563a8 Email (required) b22fdcdb Job Alert 77621881 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Education & Training HEO6 Education & Training HEO6 Locations Waite (Urrbrae), SA, Australia Waite (Urrbrae), SA, Australia Portfolio College of Science College of Science Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details Please choose a portfolio"
