    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/bioinformatics-analyst-level-a-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Together, we will defineAdelaide University",
      "description": "Bioinformatics Analyst - Level A - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Bioinformatics Analyst - Level A Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Education & Training Level A Fixed term - Full-time Level A Add to favourites View favourites Based at SAiGENCI, College of Health 24 Month Fixed-Term contract (1 FTE) Level A - $82,838 - $111,384 per annum plus an employer contribution of 17% superannuation applies. At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are looking for an exceptional Bioinformatics Analyst to bring strong expertise in biostatistics, data science, and computational analysis to our innovative research programs. Working alongside leading researchers and multidisciplinary teams, you’ll help uncover new insights from complex biological data and develop computational approaches that advance our understanding of cancer. You’ll have the opportunity to work at the intersection of biology, data science, and technology, helping translate cutting-edge research into meaningful scientific discoveries. Work that matters The Data Sciences Unit within the Computational Systems Oncology program at the South Australian immunoGENomics Cancer Institute (SAiGENCI) is responsible for data stewardship and provides core biostatistical support, as well as enabling the design, analysis, and interpretation of complex biomedical data with a strong focus on integrative and translational research. The Unit has expertise in the management and analysis of multi-omics datasets, including genomics, proteomics, lipidomics, and metabolomics, and works closely with researchers to ensure robust study design, reproducibility, and statistical inference. With access to state-of-the-art resources and a supportive, collaborative environment, this position provides an excellent platform for professional growth and the chance to make a real impact in the field of biological and cancer research. The team The role is ideal for candidates with a strong background in data analysis, statistics, bioinformatics, and computational biology, who are excited to apply rigorous analytical and statistical approaches to real biological and biomedical problems. Support and mentorship will be provided to help strong quantitative researchers further develop their biological and bioinformatics expertise and apply their skills effectively in a Bioinformatics Analyst role. Visit the AU website to learn more about SAiGENCI Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is ideal for someone who thrives in a collaborative and innovative environment with international visibility, and high-impact, conceptually driven cancer research. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experiences A Master's or PhD in statistics, biostatistics, data science, computer science, bioinformatics or a closely related discipline strong programming skills in R or Python experience developing or applying methods to complex or large-scale datasets ability to work both independently and collaboratively within an interdisciplinary research team strong written and verbal communication skills. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Build on your career with Adelaide University now Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter that tells us why you’re excited about the role upload a document that includes your responses to all the experience criteria Submit your application by 11:30pm Sunday 13 September 2026 The University reserves the right to close this advertisement before the closing date if a suitable candidate is identified. Please note that the role description is not attached to this advertisement as it is currently being finalised. For further information about this opportunity, please contact: (quoting reference number 493398) . Evelyn Ruth Talent Acquisition Advisor +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) f8c33450 Last Name (required) 8f729a74 Email (required) c2c1333b Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 607a1306 Last Name (required) 0bcfb970 Email (required) 1c76f5a9 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Senior Lecturer - Psychology Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Psychology Provide clinical oversight, assessment and support for Master of Psychology students undertaking placements Technical Assistant, Hospital and Health Service Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Specialist Facilities and Technical Services - Health Help deliver technical services to support simulation and clinical teaching environments, maintain compliance with safety standards and foster a collaborative team culture. Executive Assistant Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 College Services - Science Manage executive operations, coordination and communications for senior leaders, enabling strategic delivery across the College of Science. Project Officer Waite (Urrbrae), SA, Australia, 5064 School of Agriculture, Food and Wine Coordinate a major grains research project, managing partners, milestones, reporting and stakeholder engagement across universities and industry. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 1b359099 Last Name (required) cd562df3 Email (required) ac5777d3 Job Alert c746f277 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Education & Training Level A Education & Training Level A Locations Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Portfolio College of Health College of Health Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details Please choose a portfolio"
