      "title": "Together, we will defineAdelaide University",
      "description": "Senior Business Development Manager, Health - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Senior Business Development Manager, Health Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO9 Continuing - Full-time HEO9 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Be part of the Industry and Government team in the International and External Engagement portfolio Full-time continuing position based at the at the City West campus Salary Range: $135,226 to $144,672 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) Join a high performing, collaborative team focused on innovation and outcomes within the Health sector At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters The Senior Business Development Manager will lead the development and management of strategic partnerships and external engagement initiatives across international and government health sectors, driving revenue growth and advancing Adelaide University’s reputation and impact through industry and government collaboration. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description above to discover more about this opportunity. The team As part of a high performing, collaborative and innovative team, this role forms part of Business Development and Industry Partnerships within the Industry and Government Function and is aligned to the International and External Engagement Portfolio within the University. Visit the AU website to learn more about the International and External Engagement portfolio. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Demonstrated experience in developing and managing strategic relationships with industry and government stakeholders, achieving revenue targets Experience in providing strategic advice and guidance to internal stakeholders regarding business and product development Proven ability to develop and implement strategic plans, generate income, and provide leadership in business development within higher education or industry Experience in market development, opportunity assessment, and protection of intellectual property Experience in executing commercial project proposals, including negotiation, budget development, risk management, and contract compliance Experience within and strong understanding of the industry, professional, and government environments in Australia and internationally Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now 