    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/senior-manager-inclusion-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Together, we will defineAdelaide University",
      "description": "Senior Manager, Inclusion - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Senior Manager, Inclusion Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO9 Management Continuing - Full-time HEO9 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in the Organisational Capability function, People & Culture, City West Campus Part-time or Full time, continuing position Salary Range: $135,226 – 144,672 per annum plus 17% superannuation At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters The Senior Manager, Inclusion provides strategic leadership to a specialist team, building capability through mentorship, support and development, while leading the delivery of a whole-of-University Inclusion, Diversity, Equity, Allyship and Storytelling (IDEAS) strategy. The role will drive the integration of IDEAS principles across policy, practice and culture, strengthening inclusion, equity and belonging through strategic engagement, education, storytelling and allyship initiatives. As a trusted advisor, you will provide expert guidance and thought leadership, leveraging data and evidence to inform decision-making, measure impact and drive continuous improvement. The role is equally focused on strengthening engagement, belonging and participation across the University community, while ensuring effective governance, compliance and reporting frameworks are in place. Through strategic partnerships and a proactive, evidence-informed approach, you will help position Adelaide University as a sector leader in advancing inclusive excellence and meeting its regulatory and organisational obligations. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description above to discover more about this opportunity. The team Reporting to the Executive Director, Organisational Capability, you will collaborate closely with University leaders, the IDEAS team, Organisational Capability and Safer Community colleagues, and external partners to embed inclusive practices and drive meaningful cultural change across the institution. The role sits within Organisational Capability, a strategic function responsible for shaping the employee experience and enabling organisational success. Through leadership development, inclusion, culture, engagement and learning initiatives, the team builds capability, fosters belonging and supports a thriving University community Visit the AU website to learn more about People & Culture. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys variety and connecting with people. Each day brings a diverse range of interactions, making the work engaging, dynamic, and rewarding. The Inclusion team typically works together in a shared office environment, which can be lively during peak periods. However, there is flexibility to work in an alternative setting as needed, particularly for tasks that require greater focus and concentration. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Strong leadership and people management skills, with experience leading, mentoring and developing high-performing teams. Proven experience developing and delivering strategic inclusion, diversity and equity initiatives, with a focus on achieving meaningful and measurable outcomes. Strong knowledge of best practice in diversity, inclusion, allyship and equity, with a demonstrated commitment to role modelling and fostering inclusive and equitable workplaces. Excellent stakeholder engagement and influencing skills, with the ability to build trusted relationships, collaborate with diverse groups and generate buy-in for strategic initiatives. Strong analytical, problem-solving and communication skills, with the ability to interpret data, translate insights into action and communicate effectively to inform decision-making and drive change. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter that tells us why you’re excited about the role The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Sunday 6 September 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493464): Jessica Maslen Team Lead, Talent Acquisition, People & Culture +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #S-DNI #LI-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 250d6b09 Last Name (required) 1877bc6d Email (required) b80f9ad1 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 33860dd4 Last Name (required) c7cb57e6 Email (required) 75928594 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Senior Lecturer - Psychology Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Psychology Provide clinical oversight, assessment and support for Master of Psychology students undertaking placements Technical Assistant, Hospital and Health Service Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Specialist Facilities and Technical Services - Health Help deliver technical services to support simulation and clinical teaching environments, maintain compliance with safety standards and foster a collaborative team culture. Executive Assistant Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 College Services - Science Manage executive operations, coordination and communications for senior leaders, enabling strategic delivery across the College of Science. Project Officer Waite (Urrbrae), SA, Australia, 5064 School of Agriculture, Food and Wine Coordinate a major grains research project, managing partners, milestones, reporting and stakeholder engagement across universities and industry. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 72f7b888 Last Name (required) d5d8dd08 Email (required) 01e99d21 Job Alert d53e1a77 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories HEO9 Management HEO9 Management Locations Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Portfolio People and Culture People and Culture Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details Please choose a portfolio"
