    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/data-engineer-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Together, we will defineAdelaide University",
      "description": "Data Engineer - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Data Engineer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Engineering HEO7 Fixed term - Full-time HEO7 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in the Business Intelligence team at the City West campus Full-time 24 month fixed term contract Salary Range: $103,719 - $116,002 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) Ensure the integrity, accessibility, and quality of data assets At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Enable data-driven decision-making by designing, developing, and maintaining robust data pipelines, models, and solutions that support the Adelaide University’s strategic and operational objectives. The role ensures the integrity, accessibility, and quality of data assets to empower business intelligence and analytics across the institution. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description below to discover more about this opportunity. The team This role forms part of Business Intelligence team within the Performance, Data and Insights Function and is aligned to the Corporate Portfolio within the University. The Data Engineer will work most closely with the Chief Data and Analytics Officer, Director, Business Intelligence, and the IT and Finance teams. Visit the AU website to learn more about the Corporate Portfolio . Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Experience in data manipulation, preparation, and integration Experience in designing, developing, and supporting data pipelines, models, and processes Proficiency in data management and business intelligence concepts and practices Experience with data manipulation tools and/or programming languages such as Power Query, Alteryx, SQL, and R Experience in stakeholder engagement, expectations, and relationship management Advanced Microsoft Office skills Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Sunday 13 September 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493457): Alexandra Koszegi Team Lead, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) b442e4c3 Last Name (required) 34f15a44 Email (required) 7c6a6803 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 1f723f7d Last Name (required) 848ceda1 Email (required) daee0459 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Senior Lecturer - Psychology Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Psychology Provide clinical oversight, assessment and support for Master of Psychology students undertaking placements Technical Assistant, Hospital and Health Service Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Specialist Facilities and Technical Services - Health Help deliver technical services to support simulation and clinical teaching environments, maintain compliance with safety standards and foster a collaborative team culture. Executive Assistant Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 College Services - Science Manage executive operations, coordination and communications for senior leaders, enabling strategic delivery across the College of Science. Project Officer Waite (Urrbrae), SA, Australia, 5064 School of Agriculture, Food and Wine Coordinate a major grains research project, managing partners, milestones, reporting and stakeholder engagement across universities and industry. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) df99a5c8 Last Name (required) beb52a03 Email (required) 6adf199c Job Alert 045a5ce6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Engineering HEO7 Engineering HEO7 Locations Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Adelaide CBD, SA, Au